# Golden Thread cache and recorded evidence. Disposable: `verify` rebuilds the
# evidence, the manifest rebuilds the policy cache.
.golden-thread/

# golden-thread-attestations.json IS COMMITTED IN A REAL PROJECT, and this line
# is the exception, not the rule. An attestation is the one artefact nothing
# can regenerate, and it has to travel to a CI runner that would otherwise
# report agreed work as un-agreed.
#
# It is ignored *here* because this project is a demonstration: its
# attestations are produced by demo/run-dod-demo.sh against a mission the demo
# itself rewrites, so a committed snapshot would be stale the moment the demo
# ran. A real project commits this file and reviews it in the merge request --
# which is where "who attested what, about which version" belongs.
golden-thread-attestations.json

# golden-thread.json is NOT ignored, and that is the point: the manifest is
# what pins the golden path for everyone on the team, including a CI runner
# with no developer to run `init` for it. It became committable when the
# manifest learned to hold a source relative to the project -- until then it
# carried an absolute path specific to one machine.

.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
